From 6431e33307f883f6c91d72bec05e2870429a892a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:03:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Aurora: sun shadows from a shadow map, so what is off screen
 still casts (off by default)

The HD look's sun shadows came from the screen: a step toward the sun that
left the screen counted as lit, so a building beside Link, out of view, cast
nothing, and walking between buildings put him back in the sun.

With aurora_set_sun_shadow_map(true) (or DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP=1) and sun
shadows on, each EFB pass's solid draws are drawn again from the sun into a
2048x2048 depth map before the pass, the frame's first pass clearing it. Every
gxcore draw keeps its transforms in its constants and has the one decoded
vertex layout, so two pipelines draw them all (positions through the current
matrix, or the per-vertex ones), with the draw's own constants and the camera's
view space taken to the map by one matrix: nothing is compiled per draw. In an
in-between frame the draws take their blended constants and the map that
frame's camera. A caster writes depth and colour, is not blended, is triangles
and keeps every pixel; alpha-tested leaves and fences are left out (the map has
no textures) and keep a few of the screen's steps.

The sun shadow pass then takes each pixel's place in the world to the map and
filters nine lookups there. The map covers 5000 world units around a point
ahead of the camera, moved by whole texels so its edges don't crawl.
DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP_SIZE, _RANGE, _DEPTH, _BIAS and _CONTACT tune it,
_DEBUG=1 shows its shadow alone and _TRACE=1 logs its casters.

render() takes the HD look's camera once for each frame it encodes
(frame_camera), as the map and the effects both need it. The part of render()
that picks a draw's in-between ranges is collect_parts(), shared with the map.


The commits since, squashed into this patch (be07338..6431e33):

- b5f97e0bf9 Aurora: the sun shadow map's screen steps leave out what the map holds
- d0e3b56450 local debug: F3 dumps the next frames (DOL_AURORA_FRAME_INTERP_DUMP_KEY)
- d9f8b251c9 Aurora: with the sun shadow map on, the game's own shadows are left out
- dbebefa4f7 Aurora: the sun shadow map's shadows at the scene's size, without the screen's steps
- c874b6f741 Aurora: the sun shadow map filters a turned disc of lookups
- 4268c62211 local debug: DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP_DEBUG=2 shows the map itself as contour bands
- 7b4a9af4ea local test: DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_MAP_ALL lets alpha-tested draws cast, solid
- 4751fc8ce0 Aurora: alpha-tested scenery casts its texture's cutout into the sun shadow map
- fdc3269fff local debug: DOL_AURORA_SUN_CASTER_LOG says why a scope's draws cast or not
- 4ca198351b Aurora: the sail and flags cast into the sun shadow map
- 607dc37921 Aurora: the game's own shadows are left out while the sun shadow map is on
- bdeac61beb Aurora: blended furniture casts when its vertices stand still
- 6431e33307 Aurora: the sun shadow map in four cascades, and a bias for a low sun
